# TypeScript Config Presets

Shared presets live in `@repo/typescript-config`. Apps and libraries **extend** a runtime preset and never fork compiler options. The preset JSON is the source of truth for which options are set; this rule covers what the JSON cannot say. Changing a shared preset is a monorepo-wide breaking change.

| Preset | For | Runtime shape |
|--------|-----|---------------|
| `strict.json` | never extended directly | shared strict core; the flags that change how code is written are in [code-style.mdc](code-style.mdc) |
| `library.json` | cross-runtime JIT libraries (extends `strict`) | `lib: es2023`, no DOM or Worker globals; `noEmit` + incremental `tsBuildInfoFile` |
| `workers.json` | Worker apps | thin role alias of `library.json` |
| `vite-react.json` | React SPAs (extends `strict`) | `lib` includes `DOM`, `types: ["vite/client"]`; `noEmit` |
| `vite-node.json` | Vite build-time config only (extends `strict`) | `types: ["node"]`, no DOM; `noEmit` |
| `tests.json` | **mixin** appended after a runtime preset | no `lib` / `target`; tests tsbuildinfo path, `tests/` + `src/` include, exclude |

## Deliberate omissions

- **No preset-level `types` for Workers.** Each Worker app sets `"types": []` and includes `cloudflare.config.ts` and `.cloudflare/types`: the generated file carries `Env` and the workerd runtime types, and the empty list stops TypeScript auto-loading every visible `@types/*` - `@types/node`, installed for `vite.config.ts`, would put Node globals on Worker code. Runtime types come from `cf workers types`, never the shared preset; add `@cloudflare/workers-types` only for a shared library with no `cloudflare.config.ts`. `allowImportingTsExtensions` lives in `library.json`, `vite-node.json`, and `vite-react.json` (all `noEmit`): `cloudflare.config.ts` imports its entrypoint as `./src/index.ts`, and `@repo/enums-common` imports its own modules with `.ts` extensions so Node can load it natively from `cloudflare.config.ts`.
- **`isolatedDeclarations` is off**: `@repo/dtos-common` uses schema-first inference (`z.infer<typeof Schema>`), and the flag would demand a hand-written duplicate type on every exported schema ([contracts.mdc](../contracts/contracts.mdc)).

## Typecheck model (no project references)

- Internal packages are Just-in-Time: `exports` point at source `.ts`, with no declaration emit. Typecheck is `tsc --noEmit` per package, orchestrated by Turborepo's transit node. Never add Project References, `composite`, or a root solution `tsconfig.json`: Turborepo owns the graph.
- Apps split build-time config into `tsconfig.node.json` (`vite-node.json`) - `vite.config.ts`, plus `vitest.config.ts` and the assets-only `cloudflare.config.ts` in `front-app` - so `src/**` never inherits Node globals; React SPAs also split `tsconfig.json` → `tsconfig.app.json`. `worker-api` keeps `cloudflare.config.ts` in its main (Worker) project, because the generated `.cloudflare/types/index.d.ts` imports it to infer `Env`. `check-types` runs every project with `tsc --noEmit -p ...`.
- Tests are a separate project per package at `tests/tsconfig.json`, with array `extends`: the package's own base first, then `@repo/typescript-config/tests.json`. Keep that path and filename: editor lookup walks up for a file named exactly `tsconfig.json`, and each root config includes `src/**` only, so a root-level `tsconfig.test.json` would leave test files in no project (IDE breaks while `tsc -p` in CI still passes).
- `include` replaces rather than merges across `extends`, so a package adding roots (`.tsx`, `vitest.setup.ts`, `.cloudflare/types`) respells the full list with `${configDir}` prefixes.

## Editing rules

- Extend, don't fork: `"extends": "@repo/typescript-config/…"`, adding only the overrides you must (typically `compilerOptions.types` and `include`). Never copy compiler options into an app, and never set `strict: false` to clear errors.
- Keep presets path-agnostic with `${configDir}`: never hardcode paths, and never add `paths` or `imports` to a shared preset.
- Runtime concerns stay in their runtime preset: `jsx` and the DOM `lib` belong in `vite-react.json`, never `workers.json` (Workers have no browser APIs); `@types/node` belongs to `tsconfig.node.json`, never `workers.json`. Never drop `"types": []` from a Worker tsconfig.
- Every package running `check-types` lists `"typescript": "catalog:"` in devDependencies.
- Verify repo-wide: `pnpm check-types` from the repo root, and every app still passes.

## In-app absolute imports

Node.js subpath imports in the app's `package.json`, never `compilerOptions.paths`:

```json
{
  "imports": {
    "#/*": [
      "./src/*",
      "./src/*.ts",
      "./src/*.tsx",
      "./src/*/index.ts",
      "./src/*/index.tsx"
    ]
  }
}
```

```ts
import { Button } from "#/components/ui/Button";
```

Vite resolves `package.json` `"imports"` natively: never mirror the map in `vite.config.ts`.
